{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica","id":1306275,"title":"Tremere Perdo Magica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-20T10:18:58-07:00","id":1306275,"title":"Tremere Perdo Magica","content":"Don't you guys think that Tremere counter-magic is way too powerful against mages? I mean, in most cases the Tremere is going to roll more dice to counter the spell than the Willworker. So basicaly I think that a powerful Tremere almost always get the upper hand when dealing with mages, what I sometimes think is too OP. How to deal with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:32:32-07:00","id":1306279,"title":"","content":"See how many dice he rolls at Noon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T10:49:03-07:00","id":1306281,"title":"","content":"With the right rituals, just as many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T12:47:01-07:00","id":1306306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306281#post1306281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the right rituals, just as many.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For 12 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:34:02-07:00","id":1306329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306306#post1306306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For 12 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well with a level 1 rituai that is, in any case that's not the point of the thread one would assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T15:53:42-07:00","id":1306351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306329#post1306329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well with a level 1 rituai that is, in any case that's not the point of the thread one would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its the only one available that lets them break their humanity cap. If you are going to go with &quot;Well they could make up any ritual they need&quot; then of course the Tremere always win. There are a variety of costs built into Blood magic like you know being a vampire.. like how they can't spend extra blood to make their paths more powerful. Like how they can't really alter rituals on the fly.. That some of them are really good at not being magiced is a thing.. that''s all that path does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T16:43:40-07:00","id":1306360,"title":"","content":"I know the limitations of blood magic, the thing is I think Tremere Counter Spell makes them perhaps too good at countering mage's powers, specially when one take into consideration that they don't need to worry about paradox etc. And yes there are basically rituals for many different things, including making paths more powerful or to allow a Tremere to use blood as a mage use quintessence to reduce the difficult of their spells etc. But I'm not comparing them, because everything depends on the situation, the individuals involved usw., but just making an observation that they can easily be much better than expected at fighting mages, something that does not always come to mind when you think of it.<br /> <br /> In any case I'm just really worried about one of my players that said he would invest heavily in Perdo Magica and he has many mages enemies (it's a dark ages game, massasa war happening etc). So I was wondering about these issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:02:00-07:00","id":1306370,"title":"","content":"Vampires are greatly disadvantaged during the day, but you're typically going to encounter Vampires at night (unless you're actively pursuing one via Correspondence or other tracking methods, which is simple for some Mages and hard for others). It's almost like saying &quot;I know this character has 15 dice to dodge at difficulty 3, but that's not going to do them much good if I attack them while they're asleep.&quot; All defenses are situational.<br /> <br /> As for blood mage countermagic, if you don't want it to work on magick then just say it doesn't work. Or say that it only works in specific instances; Tremere countering a Hermetic could work, but their thaumaturgical countermagic will be useless against a Dreamspeaker or a Akashayana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:06:36-07:00","id":1306371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306360#post1306360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case I'm just really worried about one of my players that said he would invest heavily in Perdo Magica and he has many mages enemies (it's a dark ages game, massasa war happening etc). So I was wondering about these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST everything that the players get it something you've permitted. You're the final arbiter. If you don't like a PC having a certain path, you can say no. I find &quot;No, but-&quot; is a strong tool for a storyteller. Give them something else (that they pay for with EXP and freebies of course) which runs along similar lines and lets them enjoy playing.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, you can't have countermagic since it's so powerful in this context, but I'd be happy for you to have a Mage Retainer, so long as you put enough points in and it's all RP'd properly; I'm thinking a power-hungry infatuated apprentice who is generally loyal but not exactly &quot;obedient&quot;&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is far more interesting for a story than &quot;I block spells well&quot;. Now you're got a traitor on your side who is connected to both sides of the Massassa War, who can protect you from magick if you manipulate his blood bond correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:14:36-07:00","id":1306375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306360#post1306360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In any case I'm just really worried about one of my players that said he would invest heavily in Perdo Magica and he has many mages enemies (it's a dark ages game, massasa war happening etc). So I was wondering about these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he have no Kindred foes? The mages convincing some Brujah beat stick to handle their problem for you favors is pretty easy there. Perdo does jack shit againt spirits or any other summoned entities and I can't remember if it does anything at all to enchanted items. It just helps.. in the spur of the moment fast casting and MIGHT unweave rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:21:42-07:00","id":1306380,"title":"","content":"Yeah everything is situational as I said in the previous post. But back to topic,. I wouldn't say it doesn't work because that would be perhaps to harsh a measure as the RAW say it works this way, I don't want to sound unfair to the player, after all he lost his last character like 7 sessions ago.<br /> The rules also cover the fact that against different paradigms, i.e. not hermetic ones, the dice pool is halved (but is still considerable as it means 5 dice against the mage's Arete). The only option I'm really considering is making it works with the halved dice pool against any true magick, including hermetic. In any case the character is only concerned with hermetic as the Tremere are at war with them, so other paradigms are of no concern at this point in the chronicle at least. I posted here to hear different opinion as I don't really want to sound unfair to my players, so it's good to see different views on the issue.<br /> <br /> Cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:28:22-07:00","id":1306382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306375#post1306375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does he have no Kindred foes? The mages convincing some Brujah beat stick to handle their problem for you favors is pretty easy there. Perdo does jack shit againt spirits or any other summoned entities and I can't remember if it does anything at all to enchanted items. It just helps.. in the spur of the moment fast casting and MIGHT unweave rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ofc he does, but things are not so simple. With all due respect, I'm not here asking for tips for storytelling as I'm storytelling for more than 20 years...not that it necessarily mean much I know, but my point is just to discuss the issue I brought up. I just want to know if people think like me or perhaps have different opinions so that I can perhaps change my mind and not think it's too powerful etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T19:14:55-07:00","id":1306391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306382#post1306382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ofc he does, but things are not so simple. With all due respect, I'm not here asking for tips for storytelling as I'm storytelling for more than 20 years...not that it necessarily mean much I know, but my point is just to discuss the issue I brought up. I just want to know if people think like me or perhaps have different opinions so that I can perhaps change my mind and not think it's too powerful etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think focusing on Defending against the obvious methods of being attacked by ones enemies is bad rp or too powerful. I think the Shere lack of versatility that Perdo Magica makes up for its power. For the same xp he could get conjuring which.. can make any item he can think of. OR he could command spirits. Or he could have dominate to command the minds of mortals and ride their bodies and both would be just as effeciive in handling NON mage problems. He's limiting his capacity to do STUFF for the sake of limited Defense options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if the only thing that the Vampire character has fighting him all the time is Mages. LIke there's NOTHING but Magic and blood magic that's coming into game. EVEN THEN I don't think Perdo Magica is that powerful. It requires active defense(unlike Parma Magica) so powers that the Blood mage does not notice he cannot defend against. Now even if you allow Perdo to protect from &quot;Surprise you're on fire&quot; which is a fair option he doesn't have an ability to detect every subtle magical effect thrown around. IF you have some how given him the ability to see other effects in action then still Mages have the capacity to bank more successes. OR they could spam magic at him. and over run his blood per turn.<br /> <br /> So if someone wants to Turtle they can Turtle. He will make it harder for mages to kill him at the price of &quot;Do anything else&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you are giving him free Rituals. That's the broken end of things not perdo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:32:35-07:00","id":1306472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306391#post1306391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think focusing on Defending against the obvious methods of being attacked by ones enemies is bad rp or too powerful. I think the Shere lack of versatility that Perdo Magica makes up for its power. For the same xp he could get conjuring which.. can make any item he can think of. OR he could command spirits. Or he could have dominate to command the minds of mortals and ride their bodies and both would be just as effeciive in handling NON mage problems. He's limiting his capacity to do STUFF for the sake of limited Defense options.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if the only thing that the Vampire character has fighting him all the time is Mages. LIke there's NOTHING but Magic and blood magic that's coming into game. EVEN THEN I don't think Perdo Magica is that powerful. It requires active defense(unlike Parma Magica) so powers that the Blood mage does not notice he cannot defend against. Now even if you allow Perdo to protect from &quot;Surprise you're on fire&quot; which is a fair option he doesn't have an ability to detect every subtle magical effect thrown around. IF you have some how given him the ability to see other effects in action then still Mages have the capacity to bank more successes. OR they could spam magic at him. and over run his blood per turn.<br /> <br /> So if someone wants to Turtle they can Turtle. He will make it harder for mages to kill him at the price of &quot;Do anything else&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you are giving him free Rituals. That's the broken end of things not perdo.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reflexive action, so if he's able to by any mean detect a spell being weaved (what isn't really hard for any creature of the night, even less so for any kind of sorcerer/mage) he can try to counter it. But in any case what you said is true, he's sacrificing a lot of versatility in favor of being able to defend himself against a single type of enemy. I think it doesn't need a &quot;nerf&quot; then. Oh and as for rituals, they're never free in my games, they almost aways cost xp or something worse, like a pact or a geas usw.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:01:20-07:00","id":1306487,"title":"","content":"You need to be specific about which version you mean. Like, V5 doesn't have paths, V20 Dark Ages didn't include countermagic, and V20 countermagic doesn't work on mages.<br /> <br /> Also, you've implied that your mages have arete and suffer paradox which isn't right, if it's in the Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:30:46-07:00","id":1306500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306487#post1306487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to be specific about which version you mean. Like, V5 doesn't have paths, V20 Dark Ages didn't include countermagic, and V20 countermagic doesn't work on mages.<br /> <br /> Also, you've implied that your mages have arete and suffer paradox which isn't right, if it's in the Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that is&quot;right&quot; is what the ST decides is &quot;right&quot;, I think you missed the point of the thread, but I'm gonna try to explain to you. Perdo Magica was published in House of Tremere and in the guide to the low clans for Dark ages vampire. In any case it's completelly linked to the Tremere lore, even if they didn't published such path in v20 dark ages (if I'm not mistaken they basically made it a ritual, but now I'm not with time to tell you where to find it, but it's absolutely irrelevant to the discussion in any case. As for V5, I ignore it completelly, at least until the present time...). But just to explain things better to you, it's implied that Thaumaturgical Counterspell doesn't work against mages anymore because nowadays their pratices, paradign etc is very different, as opposed to what it was in the Dark Ages, it's not that hard to read between the lines, specially when you're read all the books published on the subjet up to this time in your 20 years of experienc storytelling.<br /> As for refering to Arete, I'm sorry, but I didn't feel the need to explain that my mages didn't use Arete in the early part of the game, but now we're in the late 15th century and after the tradition convention usw. so now I'm using Arete with Spheres etc instead of the foundation and pillars of Dark Ages Mage.<br /> So all in all I have long ago allowed the use of the Path of Perdo Magica, so it would be at the very least strange on my part to forbidden it now, specially because the player spent exp buying points in it during the height of the massasa war. But then again, the point of the thread was to discuss if other people felt it was op or not and I have come to the conclusion that it's not. And btw to turn it into a ritual makes it even more op, so I'm glad I chose to use it as a Path as was published before.<br /> <br /> Cheers, sorry for my temperament I'm not in a very good moment to discuss such things (I'm feeling very ill), but I didn't want to let you wait for me to explain it better. See you around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-21-2019, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:49:03-07:00","id":1306503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306500#post1306500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cheers, sorry for my temperament I'm not in a very good moment to discuss such things (I'm feeling very ill), but I didn't want to let you wait for me to explain it better. See you around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, then I won't read the post then if you're not feeling right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T05:33:39-07:00","id":1306511,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019ve always thought Perdo Magica to be strong as hell in what it does, but like said it is kinda one trick pony and those exp could have been put to more generally useful powers. <br /> <br /> Still despite it\u2019s incredible strength Perdo Magica can be over powered by extended effects and rituals of Mages. And like said you need yo be able to detect the attack which is generally possible through Auspex 2, Thaumaturgy 1 combined power (if I remember the requisities correctly ) That detects magic. Otherwise you have no sure way to know if magic is really happening or their just chanting to distract you.<br /> <br /> Well you might know something is up through Awareness roll but it gives you no specifics of what is happening just that something is.<br /> <br /> All in all it is powerful in it\u2019s limited scope, it does not necessarily be able to help you every time you are targeted (like as an extreme example during the day through a correspondence spell, or as less extreme example just hit by a spell you did not notice) but whenit does it tends to work great. It is also points away from something else so in the end it kinda does balance out in the end.<br /> <br /> Though still I must admit that when I first read it in House of Tremere I too thought it way too overpowered but over the years I have started to think that perhaps, due to reasons above, it is not that overpowered afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T08:23:33-07:00","id":1306531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306472#post1306472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a reflexive action, so if he's able to by any mean detect a spell being weaved (what isn't really hard for any creature of the night, even less so for any kind of sorcerer/mage) he can try to counter it. But in any case what you said is true, he's sacrificing a lot of versatility in favor of being able to defend himself against a single type of enemy. I think it doesn't need a &quot;nerf&quot; then. Oh and as for rituals, they're never free in my games, they almost aways cost xp or something worse, like a pact or a geas usw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a reflexive action but its costs a blood and is still limited by the amount of blood he can spend per turn. The fluff also seems to indicate a need to make some sort of ritual gestures of defense. As for Creatures of the night detecting when a spell is being weaved if you See bob the mage doing something.. Yes. If suddenly a fireball is flying at you. Yes. If your Ghoul suddenly rally's their will and finally pulls you out into the sun after years of abuse... is that magic or was that just bad luck? And that i know of Kindred Don't have anything like Sense magic.. they can detect fellow blood mages and be supsicious of acts.. but if something isn't obvious they have no way of knowing. Sure they can throw blood at every odd conincidence.. but that's going to cost them. You can of course allow their magic sight combo to function on other supernatural powers but that's not the default and a specialized combo, that he can spend more xp on.<br /> <br /> This is not to say its not a worthwhile defense. Just that its more akin to buying armor before heading into battle than getting to always throw Rock when Mages throw Scissors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T08:49:31-07:00","id":1306536,"title":"","content":"Had to chime back in to confirm that @Lian is correct that Kindred have no method of sensing magic, other than general Awareness ability and Aura Perception that can see ongoing magic in the aura, as Thaumaturgical Sight, the combo power I described earlier, specifically calls out it\u2019s inability to help sense any other magic than Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> So basically they can only sense/notice obvious Magick used against them and use Perdo Magica to defend against those but subtler uses and effects will get through unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:29:47-07:00","id":1306544,"title":"","content":"While I generally thought V20 rules were an improvement on previous versions, I preferred the Revised Edition's rules for countering true magick. It made vampires as a whole a lot less invulnerable to magic, though a highly skilled blood magician who specialized in Thaumaturgical Countermagic could still bank on being able to resist it effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:47:31-07:00","id":1306628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306544#post1306544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I generally thought V20 rules were an improvement on previous versions, I preferred the Revised Edition's rules for countering true magick. It made vampires as a whole a lot less invulnerable to magic, though a highly skilled blood magician who specialized in Thaumaturgical Countermagic could still bank on being able to resist it effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, because here I'm not even mentioning the rules for resisting magic with Wits + Occult introduced in m20 that makes vampires EVEN more op against willworkers, but I don't like the idea of a creature being able to resist something it doesn't even understand to begin with. So in that sense I prefer to let my players have Perdo Magica or similar powers as at least they require knowledge (and xp investment) of the Art. And that's basically the fluf things you people that say vampires can't sense magic with thaumaturgical sight are missing, the Tremere are Hermetic, so their pratices are very similar, it would be at the very least absolutely unfair for a ST to not allow the said kindred to try to notice something familiar and &quot;wicked&quot; being thrown at him, be it with his awareness or with the good old int+ occult of older versions of the game. But all in all, I think that v20 rules made vampires way too resistant to spells, or should I say, it made it too easy to resist spells usw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T05:33:49-07:00","id":1306806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306500#post1306500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just to explain things better to you, <b>it's implied that Thaumaturgical Counterspell doesn't work against mages anymore because nowadays their pratices, paradign etc is very different</b>, as opposed to what it was in the Dark Ages, it's not that hard to read between the lines, specially when you're read all the books published on the subjet up to this time in your 20 years of experienc storytelling.<br /> As for refering to Arete, I'm sorry, but I didn't feel the need to explain that my mages didn't use Arete in the early part of the game, but<b> now we're in the late 15th century and after the tradition convention usw. so now I'm using Arete with Spheres etc instead of the foundation and pillars of Dark Ages Mage.</b><br /> So all in all I have long ago allowed the use of the Path of Perdo Magica, so it would be at the very least strange on my part to forbidden it now, specially because the player spent exp buying points in it during the height of the massasa war.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would say that changing from the Pillar System to the Arete System it's NOT a change of Practice, Paradigm, <b>etc</b>?...<br /> <br /> Historically it was a very radical change that allowed Hermetics to expand their conception of what was possible a lot (Hermetics have learned a lot of new tricks like the formely nigh-impossible warping of space and time). It's not just a &quot;weakening&quot;. You shouldn't make the effort of the 9 Traditions to build a unified langauage of magick as something that was negative to mages...<br /> <br /> And that surely sounds to me like the kind of deep changes that would make a Path not work as well as before. Imagine your player discovering that magick has<i> changed</i>, old enemies with new tricks and new allies. Tremere was <i>wrong</i> magick wasn't dying it was taking a different form that doesn't react with the same methods...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if XP sanctity it's the problem you could either offer to return the XP to him...OR allow Perdo Magica to work at half it's potency all the time (which balances with mages usually rolling half the dice, mathematically he shouldn't notice a lot...and now magick it's more versatile) <hr /><br /> And as if I feel Perdo is OP:<br /> <br /> Well, it has the same problem of all interactions with Arete system, that's the fact that the dicepools the rest of WoD use are much larger than what Mage uses, making fast-cast weaker than already is, and forcing mages to be creative OR depends on rituals (that reverses the issue).<br /> <br /> But that's a known problem of Mage crossovers in general, not about Perdo in particular. As you yourself notice, M20 rules are worse in that regards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-22-2019, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:31:52-07:00","id":1306895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306806#post1306806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would say that changing from the Pillar System to the Arete System it's NOT a change of Practice, Paradigm, <b>etc</b>?...<br /> <br /> Historically it was a very radical change that allowed Hermetics to expand their conception of what was possible a lot (Hermetics have learned a lot of new tricks like the formely nigh-impossible warping of space and time). It's not just a &quot;weakening&quot;. You shouldn't make the effort of the 9 Traditions to build a unified langauage of magick as something that was negative to mages...<br /> <br /> And that surely sounds to me like the kind of deep changes that would make a Path not work as well as before. Imagine your player discovering that magick has<i> changed</i>, old enemies with new tricks and new allies. Tremere was <i>wrong</i> magick wasn't dying it was taking a different form that doesn't react with the same methods...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if XP sanctity it's the problem you could either offer to return the XP to him...OR allow Perdo Magica to work at half it's potency all the time (which balances with mages usually rolling half the dice, mathematically he shouldn't notice a lot...and now magick it's more versatile) <hr /><br /> And as if I feel Perdo is OP:<br /> <br /> Well, it has the same problem of all interactions with Arete system, that's the fact that the dicepools the rest of WoD use are much larger than what Mage uses, making fast-cast weaker than already is, and forcing mages to be creative OR depends on rituals (that reverses the issue).<br /> <br /> But that's a known problem of Mage crossovers in general, not about Perdo in particular. As you yourself notice, M20 rules are worse in that regards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are surely right about the big change in paradigm and I didn't have the intention of making the traditions convention to sound as something negative (perhaps it's just that I love so much the system of Dark Ages Mage lol). In any case, I think the best solution is to make Perdo Magica half efficient against hermetic magick from now on. In general I'm just worried about not sounding too harsh with my players usw. <br /> Yes I agree that M20 didn't make things any better for mages in crossovers, overall it seemed to me that the M20 line in general really wanted to make mages look weaker etc (just because maybe vampires and werewolves weren't already op enough lol...), but in any case that's what house rules are for lol. Thanks for sharing your view with me. Bye for now. <br /> <br /> PS: Is Aleph really your name? I was ALMOST named Aleph, but for some reason my parents changed their plans when I was born. I think it's a really cool name, but I remember my father saying something like it was perhaps &quot;too jewish&quot; rofl. In any case I really love the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:42:53-07:00","id":1306922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1306895#post1306895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just worried about not sounding too harsh with my players usw.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very reasonable worry. I think that the explanation it's reasonable enough, and I wouldn't mind receiving it myself. Altrough I probably would ask for a chance to research this mysterious new type of magick to build better defenses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...<br /> <br /> ...If you feel like you're taking dice from the hand of your player, you may switch instead to Revised optional rule of rolling Arete + Sphere for the mages (ST:Handbook). That way you're not nerfing the player directly, but merely making a choice about the setting rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Aleph really your name? I was ALMOST named Aleph, but for some reason my parents changed their plans when I was born. I think it's a really cool name, but I remember my father saying something like it was perhaps &quot;too jewish&quot; rofl. In any case I really love the name. </div> </div> </div>Nop. I'm called Ivan.<br /> <br /> But it IS cool and has many possible correlations. It is the first letter of the jewish alphabet, a transfinite number, a tale of Jorge Luis Borges where he explores the theme of the infinite (and a good read for the concept of the Correspondence Point), and a canon NPC of the Technocracy (I didn't knew that at the moment of choosing the name, but I'm cool with it, I like General Aleph character)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:54:23-07:00","id":1306969,"title":"","content":"Perdo specifically counts itself as half as effective against Other blood magic types and other Magic types. I would not consider the change from Pillars to spheres at least that radical and force it to half numbers to keep the situation in tact.<br /> <br /> I personally would never use the &quot;Nightfolk counter magic&quot; setup used in M20. I would instead probably try to build on the &quot;using abilities to make magick more effective&quot; setup to allow anyone(even sleepers) to make magic more difficult by working with the character's Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T00:49:38-07:00","id":1307168,"title":"","content":"Summary -<br /> So, against Hermetic Magic; double your rating in dice. (At a difficulty of the effect) Against non Hermetic, It's half the dice.<br /> You can only target powers the same or lesser than your rank AND only at 5 can you influence things not directly targeting you. It costs a blood, so you're limited on the number of times it can be used a turn, even though it is reflexive.<br /> It's considered out of Clan, so 80 XP to get to a point where you get the full benefits, even for Tremere.<br /> What can a mage do with a bonus 80 XP, considering all of them can counter intrinsically*?<br /> <br /> It's literally the reason that the Tremere Vampires survived the Massala war, so it makes sense that it works pretty well, but it doesn't &quot;Win&quot;<br /> - A prepared spell could have enough successess bound in to win, because it was prepared in advance with help.<br /> <br /> *With all out defense you'll never win, you need to be able to attack.<br /> *Awareness can let Vampires sense &quot;Something&quot; is happening, but again, mages have the advantage on senses with Magic Wars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","user":"Illithid","date":". 04-23-2019, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T03:10:39-07:00","id":1307189,"title":"","content":"Where does it say its out of clan? V<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A where its Perdo which is what we are talking about treats it as another path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:51:41-07:00","id":1307366,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgical Counter Magic explicitly states it's an out of clan discipline, but you know what; in House of Tremere, it describes it as a Path. I don't have low clans near by to check that version though.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the conundrum of the OP - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> - You could take the development of Spheres from Pillars to be the &quot;Altered Practices&quot; event that changes how it functions, if that's what's needed to fix the game. It's still pretty useful against Vampire-Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:12:46-07:00","id":1307379,"title":"","content":"So as far as I know, and this is based on what it says in blood treachery, thaumaturgical counter magic is only effective when it is being used as a defence against classical, high ritual hermetic style magic, and it has absolutely no defensive properties against any form of magic that does not conform to the hermetic paradigm, which is what the thaumaturgy of clan Tremere is based on. Check this out if you\u2019re interested, I\u2019d actually like to see what other people have to say about this because I am intrigued on some opinions out there. I do allowthe thaumaturgical counter magic have to be used to do 1 to 1 successes on resisted role, but it\u2019s only effective against Glasgow high ritual hermetic style magic, which is to be frank, not exactly common, even among the order of Hermes, in the modern era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 04-23-2019, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:08:09-07:00","id":1307393,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a> Perdo Magic as in House of Tremere explicitly helps against non hermetic at half capacity 1 dice per level instead of 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T20:50:25-07:00","id":1307673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1306275-tremere-perdo-magica?p=1307366#post1307366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgical Counter Magic explicitly states it's an out of clan discipline, but you know what; in House of Tremere, it describes it as a Path. I don't have low clans near by to check that version though.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the conundrum of the OP - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> - You could take the development of Spheres from Pillars to be the &quot;Altered Practices&quot; event that changes how it functions, if that's what's needed to fix the game. It's still pretty useful against Vampire-Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Guide to the Low clans says its a path. It explicitly calls out Pillars as being effective against but is half as effective against foreign blood magics and foreign practices. <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course by the Modern nights they have focused it to be more effective against Blood magic at the price of True Magick since True Magick is less common an occurance for the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:43:55-07:00","id":1308034,"title":"","content":"On a general basis I feel like thaumaturgical countermagic should not be so effective against true magick. The latter is way more powerful than the former after all. In pratical terms this matters very little though: who's going to spend Xp to buy dots in countermagic when it's so niche anyway? There's lots of paths that are way more generally useful than countermagic UNLESS the player knows the chronicle is mainly focused on Hermetics vs Blood Mages. Then and only then this becomes a real problem.<br /> <br /> So yes, this makes little sense if we consider what True Magick is but in actual games this will not be an issue 99% of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:17:53-07:00","id":1308645,"title":"","content":"1) House of Tremere is a VtDA supplement and therefore rather old and outdated.<br /> 2) If it's the Dark Ages and Massassa War I would suggest using the DA: Vampire and DA:Mage rules for conflicts between the two. Let the Mages have Foundation+Pillars rather than Arete+Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Hell in VtDA there is a Thaum Path that at lvl one allows you to add botch dice (effectivly 1's which removes successes) to a target equal to the number of successes on your roll. Not to mention Path of Warding which is broken AF. VtDA is outdated and it's supplements should be used for fluff only, not crunch IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":392,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","user":"Cadmiumcadamium","date":". 04-29-2019, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{